    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **James Wood**, who commands the highest efficiency score of 76.06. His matchup against Grant Holmes is ideal; Holmes's high xERA of 4.71, combined with **James Wood**\u2019s elite 0.423 xwOBA and the strategic boost of hitting leadoff, positions him as our clear primary driver for counting stats. **Tyler Soderstrom** also presents a high-ceiling play at 67.73. Despite facing a formidable arm in Sonny Gray, **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a 10% park factor bump and a favorable platoon dynamic, allowing him to outperform the baseline even while hitting in the cleanup spot. **Josh Naylor** rounds out our top-tier targets at 66.05, as the combination of a wind-aided environment and a favorable platoon split against Roki Sasaki makes him a high-leverage start in the UTIL slot.\n\nDeciding between our middle-of-the-pack options required balancing raw projection against the scarcity of steals. **Seiya Suzuki** leads the marginal group with a 58.84, buoyed significantly by an 8% order advantage as the #2 hitter and the opportunity to exploit a slow delivery from Pallante, which heightens his stolen base probability. Conversely, **Austin Riley** and **Dalton Rushing** represent our most precarious starts. **Austin Riley** (54.46) was nearly displaced from the lineup due to his projected #8 spot, which heavily anchors his run production, though he remains active to keep our offensive volume high. **Dalton Rushing** (44.75) sits right on the edge of our starting floor; while the wind-out conditions at his park provide a slight safety net, his bottom-of-the-order assignment against the tough Bryan Woo makes him the most likely candidate for an early pull if we reach our game caps.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant due to a combination of scheduling quirks and health concerns. **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak** are unavailable today due to team off-days, while **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains sidelined on the IL. Given that **Jose Caballero** was excluded from his team's confirmed starting lineup, our depth is severely tested; had **Jose Caballero** been active, his profile as a potential stolen base contributor would have pushed **Dalton Rushing** to the bench to preserve our efficiency metrics. We are proceeding with caution regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Cole Young**, **Austin Riley**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Josh Naylor**, as any downward shift in their projected batting orders will necessitate a rapid reassessment of their daily efficiency scores.",
